<title>CHINA: Shanghai GDP to grow 12.5 - 13 percent this year.</title>
<headline>Shanghai GDP to grow 12.5 - 13 percent this year.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The gross domestic product of Shanghai, China's largest industrial and commercial city, is expected to grow by 12.5 to 13 percent to 280 billion yuan this year, the official Xinhua news agency said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The agency also said exports from the city are expected to rise by 12 percent over last year to around $13 billion.</p>
<p>It gave no other details.</p>
</text>
